{
  "slug": "d2c",
  "name": "D2c",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Turn Figma frames into production-ready code that uses your existing components, your design tokens, and your framework conventions. d2c scans your codebase, builds a design contract, then generates, screenshots, pixel-diffs, and iterates until the output matches the design. Four skills — init, build, audit, guard — cover the full lifecycle from token extraction to ongoing drift enforcement. Supports React, Vue, Svelte, Angular, Solid, and Astro.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **5 skills**.\n\n- **Skills** (5): `d2c-audit` (Audit codebase for design token drift, unused tokens, component reuse violations, library pattern violations, and accessibility issues), `d2c-build` (Build production-ready frontend code from a Figma design), `d2c-build-flow` (Build a connected multi-page Figma flow (onboarding, checkout, KYC, etc.) into production-ready frontend code: per-page components, a shared…), `d2c-guard` (Enforces design tokens, component reuse, SOLID/DRY principles, and preferred library conventions when editing frontend code), `d2c-init` (Scan your codebase to extract design tokens, detect framework, discover components, and configure preferred libraries)\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install d2c@claude-community` from `d2c-ai/d2c`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "antigravity",
    "codex"
  ],
  "pluginType": "wrapper",
  "wrapper": "skill",
  "sourceType": "community",
